            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0253" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23996: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Manzanillo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walsh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manzanillo</hi></placeName> (<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1920-05-17T11:27:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1920-05-14T11:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received May 17, 1920—11:27
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Bandits in charge Manzanillo since 11 a.m. 14th. Destroyer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thornton</hi>, Commander Stirling, arrived 4 p.m. and
                    saved town from violence. Standing by.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walsh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
